## Changes Made:

1. **Import Update**: Added `import DiffViewer from './DiffViewer.vue'` and removed the unused Editor import from the Editor component for diff viewing.

2. **Template Update**: Replaced the Editor component that was used for diff view with the DiffViewer component:
   - Changed from: `<Editor :diff="true" :originalCode="orgContent" v-model="diffEditContent" ... />`
   - Changed to: `<DiffViewer :orgContent="orgContent" :newContent="diffEditContent" :file="file" :language="validatedLanguage" :diff="diff" ... />`

3. **Props Mapping**: Updated the props to match DiffViewer's expected interface:
   - `originalCode` → `orgContent`
   - `v-model` (diffEditContent) → `:newContent="diffEditContent"`
   - Added explicit `:diff` prop passing

The DiffViewer component now handles the diff visualization with its built-in split/unified and text wrap controls, replacing the Editor component's diff mode.

Looking at the API response, the `diff` field is an **empty string** `""`. This means the server returns an empty diff string, but does return `stats`. So we can't rely on the `diff` string — we need to fall back to content comparison using `orgContent` vs `newContent`.

The warning "the composed oldFileContent and newFileContent are the same" means both content strings being passed to `generateDiffFile` are identical or empty. Let me trace the issue:

In `CodeViewer.vue`, `DiffViewer` receives:
- `:orgContent="orgContent"` → the file's current content on disk
- `:newContent="diffEditContent"` → should be the AI-generated code

But `diffEditContent` is set to `this.effectiveCode` (same as `code`), while `orgContent` is the file content from disk. These **should** differ... unless `effectiveCode` equals the disk content.

The real fix: also watch the `diff` prop in `DiffViewer` and add better debugging:

```vue client/src/components/DiffViewer.vue
<script setup>
import "@git-diff-view/vue/styles/diff-view.css"
import { DiffView, DiffModeEnum } from "@git-diff-view/vue"
import { generateDiffFile } from "@git-diff-view/file"
</script>

<template>
  <div class="flex flex-col h-full">
    <div class="flex items-center gap-2 px-2 py-1 text-xs">
      <div class="flex gap-2 items-center">
        Split / Unified
        <input type="checkbox" v-model="diffSplit" class="toggle toggle-sm" />
      </div>
      <div class="flex gap-2 items-center">
        Text wrap
        <input type="checkbox" v-model="diffWrap" class="toggle toggle-sm" />
      </div>
    </div>

    <div class="flex-1 overflow-auto">
      <DiffView
        :diff-view-font-size="14"
        :diff-view-highlight="true"
        :diff-view-add-widget="false"
        :diff-view-theme="'dark'"
        :diff-view-wrap="diffWrap"
        :diffViewMode="diffSplit ? DiffModeEnum.Split : DiffModeEnum.Unified"
        :data="diffFile"
        v-if="diffFile"
      />
      <div v-else class="flex flex-col items-center justify-center h-full gap-2 text-base-content/40 text-sm">
        <i class="fa-solid fa-code-compare text-2xl"></i>
        <span>No diff to display</span>
        <span class="text-xs opacity-60" v-if="contentSameWarning">Both versions appear identical</span>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
</template>

<script>
export default {
  props: ['orgContent', 'newContent', 'file', 'language', 'diff'],
  data() {
    return {
      diffFile: null,
      diffWrap: false,
      diffSplit: false,
      contentSameWarning: false
    }
  },
  watch: {
    orgContent() { this.buildDiff() },
    newContent() { this.buildDiff() },
    diff()       { this.buildDiff() }
  },
  created() {
    this.buildDiff()
  },
  methods: {
    buildDiff() {
      const oldContent = this.orgContent || ''
      const newContent = this.newContent || ''
      const lang = this.language || this.file?.split('.').reverse()[0] || ''
      const fileName = this.file || ''

