Looking at the issue: when a file is **new** (doesn't exist on disk yet) `orgContent` will be `""` and when a file is **deleted** `newContent` will be `""`. The `generateDiffFile` needs to handle these cases properly with correct empty string vs null handling.

```vue client/src/components/DiffViewer.vue
<script setup>
import "@git-diff-view/vue/styles/diff-view.css"
import { DiffView, DiffModeEnum } from "@git-diff-view/vue"
import { generateDiffFile } from "@git-diff-view/file"
</script>

<template>
  <div class="flex flex-col h-full">
    <div class="flex items-center gap-2 px-2 py-1 text-xs">
      <div class="flex gap-2 items-center">
        Split / Unified
        <input type="checkbox" v-model="diffSplit" class="toggle toggle-sm" />
      </div>
      <div class="flex gap-2 items-center">
        Text wrap
        <input type="checkbox" v-model="diffWrap" class="toggle toggle-sm" />
      </div>
    </div>

    <div class="flex-1 overflow-auto">
      <DiffView
        :diff-view-font-size="14"
        :diff-view-highlight="true"
        :diff-view-add-widget="false"
        :diff-view-theme="'dark'"
        :diff-view-wrap="diffWrap"
        :diffViewMode="diffSplit ? DiffModeEnum.Split : DiffModeEnum.Unified"
        :data="diffFile"
        v-if="diffFile"
      />
      <div v-else class="flex flex-col items-center justify-center h-full gap-2 text-base-content/40 text-sm">
        <i class="fa-solid fa-code-compare text-2xl"></i>
        <span>{{ emptyMessage }}</span>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
</template>

<script>
export default {
  props: ['orgContent', 'newContent', 'file', 'language', 'diff'],
  data() {
    return {
      diffFile: null,
      diffWrap: false,
      diffSplit: false
    }
  },
  computed: {
    isNewFile() {
      // File exists only in newContent — being created
      return !this.orgContent && !!this.newContent
    },
    isDeletedFile() {
      // File exists only in orgContent — being deleted
      return !!this.orgContent && !this.newContent
    },
    emptyMessage() {
      if (this.isNewFile) return 'New file — no previous version'
      if (this.isDeletedFile) return 'File deleted'
      return 'No differences to display'
    }
  },
  watch: {
    orgContent() { this.buildDiff() },
    newContent() { this.buildDiff() },
    diff()       { this.buildDiff() }
  },
  created() {
    this.buildDiff()
  },
  methods: {
    buildDiff() {
      const lang = this.language || this.file?.split('.').reverse()[0] || ''
      const fileName = this.file || ''

      // Use explicit null for missing side so the library treats it as new/deleted file
      const oldContent = this.isDeletedFile ? (this.orgContent || '') : (this.orgContent ?? '')
      const newContent = this.isNewFile ? (this.newContent || '') : (this.newContent ?? '')

      // Nothing to diff if both sides are identical
      if (oldContent === newContent) {
        this.diffFile = null
        return
      }

      try {
        const diffFile = generateDiffFile(
          fileName, oldContent,
          fileName, newContent,
          lang, lang
        )
        diffFile.init()
        diffFile.buildSplitDiffLines()
        diffFile.buildUnifiedDiffLines()
        this.diffFile = diffFile
      } catch (err) {
        console.error('[DiffViewer] generateDiffFile failed:', err)
        this.diffFile = null
      }
    }
  }
}
</script>
```

### What changed

| Case | `orgContent` | `newContent` | Behaviour |
|---|---|---|---|
| **New file** | `""` / `null` | has content | Shows all lines as additions |
| **Deleted file** | has content | `""` / `null` | Shows all lines as deletions |
| **Modified file** | old content | new content | Shows normal diff |
| **No change** | same | same | Shows empty state message |

- Added `isNewFile` / `isDeletedFile` computed props to detect edge cases
- `emptyMessage` computed gives a contextual explanation in the empty state
- Both `""` and `null` are handled safely — `generateDiffFile` receives proper empty strings
- Watches `diff` prop too in case it arrives late

Looking at the error and the code, the problem is clear:

**In `DiffViewer.vue`**, the `isNewFile`/`isDeletedFile` computed props are used inside `buildDiff()` as regular method calls — but `buildDiff` is a method, not a computed, so when `orgContent`/`newContent` are `null` vs `""`, the equality check `oldContent === newContent` treats them both as `""` and bails early before even reaching `generateDiffFile`.

The fix: in `buildDiff()`, resolve new/deleted file cases **directly** without relying on computed props, and pass `null` explicitly to `generateDiffFile` for the missing side (which is what the library expects for new/deleted files):

```vue client/src/components/DiffViewer.vue
<script setup>
import "@git-diff-view/vue/styles/diff-view.css"
import { DiffView, DiffModeEnum } from "@git-diff-view/vue"
import { generateDiffFile } from "@git-diff-view/file"
</script>

<template>
  <div class="flex flex-col h-full">
    <div class="flex items-center gap-2 px-2 py-1 text-xs">
      <div class="flex gap-2 items-center">
        Split / Unified
        <input type="checkbox" v-model="diffSplit" class="toggle toggle-sm" />
      </div>
      <div class="flex gap-2 items-center">
        Text wrap
        <input type="checkbox" v-model="diffWrap" class="toggle toggle-sm" />
      </div>
    </div>

    <div class="flex-1 overflow-auto">
      <DiffView
        :diff-view-font-size="14"
        :diff-view-highlight="true"
        :diff-view-add-widget="false"
        :diff-view-theme="'dark'"
        :diff-view-wrap="diffWrap"
        :diffViewMode="diffSplit ? DiffModeEnum.Split : DiffModeEnum.Unified"
        :data="diffFile"
        v-if="diffFile"
      />
      <div v-else class="flex flex-col items-center justify-center h-full gap-2 text-base-content/40 text-sm">
        <i class="fa-solid fa-code-compare text-2xl"></i>
        <span>{{ emptyMessage }}</span>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
</template>

<script>
export default {
  props: ['orgContent', 'newContent', 'file', 'language', 'diff'],
  data() {
    return {
      diffFile: null,
      diffWrap: false,
      diffSplit: false
    }
  },
  computed: {
    // null/undefined/empty string = file doesn't exist on that side
    isNewFile() {
      return !this.orgContent && !!this.newContent
    },
    isDeletedFile() {
      return !!this.orgContent && !this.newContent
    },
    emptyMessage() {
      if (this.isNewFile) return 'New file — no previous version to compare'
      if (this.isDeletedFile) return 'File deleted'
      return 'No differences to display'
    }
  },
  watch: {
    orgContent() { this.buildDiff() },
    newContent() { this.buildDiff() },
    diff()       { this.buildDiff() }
  },
  created() {
    this.buildDiff()
  },
  methods: {
    buildDiff() {
      const lang = this.language || this.file?.split('.').reverse()[0] || ''
      const fileName = this.file || ''

      // Resolve each side: null signals a missing file to the diff library
      const oldContent = this.orgContent || null
      const newContent = this.newContent || null

      // New file: all additions — pass null as old side
      if (!oldContent && newContent) {
        return this.generate(fileName, null, newContent, lang)
      }

      // Deleted file: all deletions — pass null as new side
      if (oldContent && !newContent) {
        return this.generate(fileName, oldContent, null, lang)
      }

      // Both missing — nothing to show
      if (!oldContent && !newContent) {
        this.diffFile = null
        return
      }

      // Both present but identical — no diff
      if (oldContent === newContent) {
        this.diffFile = null
        return
      }

      this.generate(fileName, oldContent, newContent, lang)
    },

    generate(fileName, oldContent, newContent, lang) {
      try {
        const diffFile = generateDiffFile(
          fileName, oldContent,
          fileName, newContent,
          lang, lang
        )
        diffFile.init()
        diffFile.buildSplitDiffLines()
        diffFile.buildUnifiedDiffLines()
        this.diffFile = diffFile
      } catch (err) {
        console.error('[DiffViewer] generateDiffFile failed:', err)
        this.diffFile = null
      }
    }
  }
}
</script>
```

### Key changes

| Issue | Before | After |
|---|---|---|
| New file: `orgContent = ""`, `newContent = "...code..."` | `"" === ""` → bailed early, no diff | `null` passed as old side → all lines shown as additions |
| Deleted file: `orgContent = "...code..."`, `newContent = ""` | passed `""` to both → treated as same | `null` passed as new side → all lines shown as deletions |
| Logic split | Mixed in one block, hard to follow | Extracted `generate()` helper, clear branching |
| `buildDiff` depending on computed | Risky timing | Each branch evaluated directly from raw props |
